## Why This Is Asked

This tests design for guardrails, data isolation, and cost controls in Azure OpenAI deployments, a common advanced requirement for regulated customers.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic safety policy engine
- Prompt redaction and blocking
- API Management routing
- Grounding with versioned KB (Blob + Cognitive Search)
- Per-tenant isolation (Cosmos DB) and quotas
- Telemetry and auditing (Data Lake)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal policy eval
function evaluatePrompt(prompt, policies) {
  for (const p of policies) {
    if (p.types?.some(t => prompt.includes(t))) {
      return {blocked: true, reason: p.reason}
    }
  }
  // simple redact example
  const redacted = prompt.replace(/SSN-\d{4}/g, '[REDACTED_SSN]')
  return {blocked: false, redacted}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant billing and quotas at API level?
- How would you test guardrails under burst traffic?

## Why This Is Asked
To assess hands-on Azure AI wiring for accessibility use cases, including voice input, multilingual output, and privacy controls, all grounded in a managed KB.

## Key Concepts
- Azure API Management as a gate
- Azure OpenAI with grounding to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Azure Speech to Text and Text to Speech
- Per-tenant language preferences
- PII redaction and interaction logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example flow tying services together
async function handleQuery(audioBlob, language) {
  const text = await speechToText(audioBlob, language);
  const answer = await openai.chat({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: text }] });
  const tts = await textToSpeech(answer.choices[0].message.content, language);
  return tts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model per-tenant language settings in Cosmos DB?
- What are the trade-offs between cloud TTS and on-device synthesis for accessibility tasks?
